          [40.0, 41.0, 41.0, 41.0, 40.0, 39.0, 38.0]
         ],
          "description": "Fine-grid surface level index per block cell, 1-based (the C++ ColumnSystemCtx::init_column m_ks + 1 = floor(H/dz) + 1 with dz = 4000/61, capped at 62; 1 for ice-free columns), the block slice of the full-field ks."
        },
        "tau": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "s",
          "shape": [
            "i",
            "j",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Fine-grid ice age (seconds; the C++ x[k] of the tridiagonal solve) on the block."
        },
        "hadv": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "i",
            "j",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Horizontal advection term u*d(tau)/dx + v*d(tau)/dy at each fine level, first-order upwind, current-time, coupled to the live neighbor columns of the block (the new 3-D coupling of this component)."
        },
        "age_storage": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "s",
          "shape": [
            "i",
            "j",
            "lev_s"
          ],
          "description": "The fine-grid solution interpolated to the 61-level storage (dump) grid (AgeModel::fine_to_coarse, the fixed linear-in-level weights (k-1)/60); the quantity the dumps carry."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "_comment": "Initial condition: the ice starts at age zero everywhere (the test run's age.initial_value = 0 years).",
          "lhs": {
            "op": "ic",
            "args": [
              "tau"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "args": [],
            "output_idx": [
              "i",
              "j",
              "k"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "i"
              },
              "j": {
                "from": "j"
              },
              "k": {
                "from": "lev"
              }
            },
            "expr": 0.0
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "The age equation d(tau)/dt = 1 - hadv - w*d(tau)/dz over the block with the AgeColumnSystem boundary conditions per column. Above the surface (k > ks) and at the surface cell (k == ks) the age stays zero (the C++ rows k > m_ks and the surface row m_ks, D = 1, RHS = 0). At the base cell (k == 1) a strictly upward bed velocity means ice is being added, so the age is pinned at zero (the C++ AA > 0 row 0); otherwise the base cell uses the interior equation with the downward upwind (the C++ AA <= 0 row 0), which reads the level above so no ghost level below the bed is touched. Interior cells 2..ks-1 carry the upwind vertical advection (implicit in the vertical in the C++ tridiagonal; here an ODE term integrated by the harness's stiff solver). The per-cell ks comes from the block-local ks_b; the vertical velocity at fine level k is the linear coarse_to_fine interpolation of the block-local padded storage-grid w3_b (age_coarse_to_fine; at the base cell k = 1 the interpolated value is exactly w3_b[i,j,1], the C++ m_w[0]). The tau_up argument of age_vertical_advection at the base cell is passed as tau[i,j,1] (safe and unused, since the base cell never enters the interior branch with w > 0; the select evaluation of the interior branch reads tau[i,j,0] as the state-array ghost zero).",
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "tau"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "args": [],
            "output_idx": [
